---
const GITHUB_URL = "https://github.com/piazzatron/rostr";
const TWITTER_URL = "https://x.com/piazzatron";
const SETUP_PROMPT = "Set up rostr for me by following the instructions at https://getroster.sh";

const ROSTER_MEMBERS = [
  { emoji: "🧙", name: "Gandalf", task: "Fix auth redirect loop", where: "rostr/api", since: "12m" },
  { emoji: "🌱", name: "Samwise", task: "Migrate billing to Stripe v3", where: "smart-notes", since: "1h" },
  { emoji: "🏹", name: "Legolas", task: "Flaky e2e tests on CI", where: "rostr/site", since: "3m" },
  { emoji: "🪓", name: "Gimli", task: "Postgres index audit", where: "cloud", since: "40m" },
];

const COMMANDS = [
  { command: "rostr create", description: "Create a roster from a preset or your own names. Choose --local or --cloud." },
  { command: "rostr draft", description: "Draft the next available agent. Your hooks run this at the start of every session." },
  { command: "rostr list", description: "See who's on your roster and what each agent is working on." },
  { command: "rostr release <name>", description: "Send an agent back to the bench when its work is done." },
  { command: "rostr edit", description: "Add, remove, or rename members, or turn emoji on and off." },
  { command: "rostr disband", description: "Delete your roster." },
];

const PRESET_ROSTERS = [
  { emoji: "💍", name: "The Fellowship", source: "The Lord of the Rings" },
  { emoji: "⚡", name: "Hogwarts", source: "Harry Potter" },
  { emoji: "🎮", name: "Smash Bros", source: "Super Smash Bros." },
  { emoji: "🐉", name: "Westeros", source: "Game of Thrones" },
  { emoji: "🌌", name: "The Rebellion", source: "Star Wars" },
  { emoji: "📎", name: "Dunder Mifflin", source: "The Office" },
  { emoji: "🔴", name: "Kanto", source: "Pokémon" },
  { emoji: "🛡️", name: "Avengers", source: "Marvel" },
  { emoji: "🖖", name: "The Enterprise", source: "Star Trek: TNG" },
  { emoji: "🎰", name: "The Crew", source: "Ocean's Eleven" },
  { emoji: "🍃", name: "Ghibli", source: "Studio Ghibli" },
  { emoji: "🏛️", name: "Olympus", source: "Greek mythology" },
];
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>rostr: give your agents names</title>
    <meta name="description" content="rostr gives each of your coding agents a name, so you can remember who's doing what. Works with Claude Code and Codex." />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="nav">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/">rostr</a>
      <nav>
        <a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a>
        <a href="#install">Install</a>
        <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <!-- Hero -->
      <section class="hero">
        <h1>Give your agents names and remember who's doing what.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          rostr drafts a name for every coding agent session you start, from a roster you pick. Gandalf is on the auth
          bug, Samwise is migrating billing, and you never have to dig through five tabs called "New session" again.
        </p>
        <div class="cta">
          <button class="copy" data-copy={SETUP_PROMPT}>
            <span class="copy-text">“{SETUP_PROMPT}”</span>
            <span class="copy-label">Copy</span>
          </button>
          <a class="button-secondary" href={GITHUB_URL}>View on GitHub</a>
        </div>
        <p class="works-with">Works out of the box with <strong>Claude Code</strong> and <strong>Codex</strong>.</p>

        <div class="terminal" aria-label="Example output of rostr list">
          <div class="terminal-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <pre><span class="prompt">$</span> rostr list
<span class="dim">fellowship · 4 of 9 drafted</span>
{ROSTER_MEMBERS.map((member) => `\n${member.emoji} ${member.name.padEnd(9)} ${member.task.padEnd(30)} ${member.where.padEnd(12)} ${member.since}`).join("")}
</pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Why -->
      <section class="section narrow">
        <h2>Think like an engineering manager</h2>
        <p>
          Running five agents at once is easy. Remembering what each one is doing is not. Every workstream you have in
          flight is something you're holding in your head, and anonymous sessions make it harder: "Untitled 4" and "Fix
          bug" tell you nothing when you come back an hour later.
        </p>
        <p>
          A good engineering manager doesn't keep a mental list of tickets. They know their team, and they know who's on
          what. Ask who's handling the billing migration and the answer is instant. rostr gives your agents that kind of
          identity, so you're checking in with Samwise about billing instead of hunting for the right terminal.
        </p>
        <p>
          Names from stories you already know work best. Samwise comes with a personality attached, so "Samwise is on
          billing" sticks in a way that "session 3" never will.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- How it works -->
      <section class="section" id="how-it-works">
        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">rostr is a small CLI plus a skill that teaches your agent how to use it.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <h3>Pick a roster</h3>
            <p>Run <code>rostr create</code> and choose one of the pre-built rosters, or bring your own list of names.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Every session gets drafted</h3>
            <p>
              When a session starts, a hook drafts the next available name and tells the agent who it is. The name goes
              at the front of the session title: <code>🧙 Gandalf · Fix auth redirect loop</code>.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Agents go back to the bench</h3>
            <p>
              The rostr skill has your agent release its name when the work is done, so the same familiar faces keep
              coming back and your roster stays small.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <!-- TODO: screenshot of named sessions in the Claude Code / Codex sidebar -->
        <figure class="screenshot-placeholder">
          <span>Screenshot: named sessions in the Claude Code sidebar</span>
        </figure>

        <div class="cards">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>💻 Local rosters</h3>
            <p>
              For sessions on your machine. Roster state lives on disk, so there's no account to make and nothing goes
              over the network.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>☁️ Cloud rosters</h3>
            <p>
              For agents running in the cloud. Sessions draft from the rostr API at <code>api.getroster.sh</code>, so
              your cloud agents share one roster and never end up with the same name.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Commands -->
      <section class="section">
        <h2>Commands</h2>
        <dl class="commands">
          {COMMANDS.map((item) => (
            <div class="command-row">
              <dt><code>{item.command}</code></dt>
              <dd>{item.description}</dd>
            </div>
          ))}
        </dl>
      </section>

      <!-- Rosters -->
      <section class="section">
        <h2>Pick your team</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          rostr comes with fun pre-built rosters, or you can make your own from any list of names. Every member gets an
          emoji; if that's not your thing, turn them off with <code>rostr edit</code>.
        </p>
        <ul class="rosters">
          {PRESET_ROSTERS.map((roster) => (
            <li>
              <span class="roster-emoji">{roster.emoji}</span>
              <span>
                <strong>{roster.name}</strong>
                <small>{roster.source}</small>
              </span>
            </li>
          ))}
          <li class="roster-custom">
            <span class="roster-emoji">✏️</span>
            <span>
              <strong>Your own</strong>
              <small>Any list of names</small>
            </span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Install -->
      <section class="section" id="install">
        <h2>Install</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Ask your agent</h3>
            <p>Point Claude Code or Codex at this page and it will install rostr, set up the hooks and skill, and help you pick a roster.</p>
            <button class="copy copy-block" data-copy={SETUP_PROMPT}>
              <span class="copy-text">“{SETUP_PROMPT}”</span>
              <span class="copy-label">Copy</span>
            </button>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Do it yourself</h3>
            <p>Install with Homebrew, create a roster, then install the hooks and skill for your agents.</p>
            <pre class="code"><span class="prompt">$</span> brew install piazzatron/tap/rostr
<span class="prompt">$</span> rostr create --preset fellowship
<span class="prompt">$</span> rostr setup <span class="dim"># hooks + skill</span></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="footer">
      <span>rostr is made by <a href={TWITTER_URL}>@piazzatron</a></span>
      <span class="footer-links">
        <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a>
        <a href={TWITTER_URL}>Twitter</a>
      </span>
    </footer>

    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy]").forEach((button) => {
        button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copy ?? "");
          const label = button.querySelector(".copy-label");
          if (!label) return;
          label.textContent = "Copied";
          setTimeout(() => (label.textContent = "Copy"), 1500);
        });
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  :root {
    --bg: #fbfaf7;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --text: #1c1b19;
    --muted: #6b675f;
    --border: #e6e2da;
    --accent: #d9480f;
    --terminal-bg: #1c1b19;
    --terminal-text: #ece8df;
    --sans: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #141312;
      --surface: #1c1b19;
      --text: #ece8df;
      --muted: #9c978d;
      --border: #2e2c29;
      --accent: #ff7a3d;
      --terminal-bg: #0d0c0b;
    }
  }

  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  a {
    color: inherit;
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.88em;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 7%, transparent);
    padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3 {
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .nav,
  main,
  .footer {
    max-width: 960px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
  }

  .nav {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding-top: 24px;
  }

  .wordmark {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 20px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .nav nav {
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .nav nav a {
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .nav nav a:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  /* Hero */
  .hero {
    padding: 72px 0 48px;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 60px);
    max-width: 14em;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 36em;
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }

  .cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .copy {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    max-width: 100%;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    font: 14px var(--mono);
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .copy:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .copy-label {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .copy-block {
    width: 100%;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .button-secondary {
    padding: 12px 18px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--text);
    color: var(--bg);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .works-with {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    margin: 16px 0 48px;
  }

  .terminal {
    background: var(--terminal-bg);
    color: var(--terminal-text);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 20px 50px -20px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.35);
  }

  .terminal-bar {
    display: flex;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 12px 14px;
  }

  .terminal-bar span {
    width: 11px;
    height: 11px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #3a3834;
  }

  .terminal pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 4px 20px 22px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font: 14px/1.7 var(--mono);
  }

  .prompt {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .dim {
    color: #8a857b;
  }

  /* Sections */
  .section {
    padding: 56px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .section h2 {
    font-size: 32px;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  .narrow p {
    max-width: 38em;
  }

  .section-lede {
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 38em;
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }

  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }

  .steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
  }

  .steps li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: white;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .steps h3 {
    margin: 12px 0 6px;
    font-size: 19px;
  }

  .steps p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .screenshot-placeholder {
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 7;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border: 2px dashed var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .card {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 24px;
  }

  .card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-size: 19px;
  }

  .card p {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .code {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 16px;
    background: var(--terminal-bg);
    color: var(--terminal-text);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font: 13px/1.7 var(--mono);
  }

  .commands {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .command-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .command-row dt code {
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .command-row dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .rosters {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .rosters li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
  }

  .rosters small {
    display: block;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .roster-emoji {
    font-size: 24px;
  }

  .roster-custom {
    border-style: dashed !important;
  }

  .footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding-top: 32px;
    padding-bottom: 48px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .footer-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .nav nav a:not(:last-child) {
      display: none;
    }

    .hero {
      padding-top: 48px;
    }

    .command-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 4px;
    }
  }
</style>
